defaultseccomp_arm64.bpf — provenance

What it is
  Docker's fixed default seccomp program, as the raw kernel struct sock_filter
  array (little-endian, 8 bytes per instruction). One filter layer, 846
  instructions, 6768 bytes. Multi-arch validation prologue for AUDIT_ARCH_AARCH64
  (0xc00000b7) and AUDIT_ARCH_ARM (0x40000028); default action SCMP_ACT_ERRNO.

Source (named)
  Docker's default profile, github.com/moby/profiles/seccomp (Apache-2.0), as
  fev's engine applies it to every default container: dockerd docker-v29.9.0
  (moby, inputs.lock), which hands the profile to runc v1.5.2, which compiles it
  to classic BPF with libseccomp v2.6.1 at the container's start. fev links no
  libseccomp (LGPL), so the compiled program is captured by dumping it from a running default container
  rather than compiled here.

Digest
  sha256 4b2732e76a6ca9d3b16fe4e782c24ea27ad239318bdd6cc635a13acd94da96df
  (6768 bytes, 846 instructions). TestDefaultSeccompIsTheRecordedCapture pins
  it, and the three versions above against inputs.lock: a bump of the engine,
  runc or libseccomp fails that test until the program is captured again
  (below) and the digest and versions here and in defaultseccomp.go are set to
  the new capture's.

How it was captured (regeneration)
  1. Start a default container (default seccomp, default capabilities) on fev's
     engine:  docker run -d --name d alpine:latest sleep 400
  2. From a sibling sharing its PID namespace, with CAP_SYS_PTRACE + CAP_SYS_ADMIN
     and seccomp unconfined, read the target init's filter stack with
     PTRACE_SECCOMP_GET_FILTER for every index until it ends (the same mechanism
     as guest/debug/attach DumpTargetStack):
       docker run --rm --pid=container:d --cap-add SYS_PTRACE --cap-add SYS_ADMIN \
         --security-opt seccomp=unconfined -v out:/out <dumper> 1
  3. Serialise filter index 0's instructions (a default container has exactly one
     layer) as the little-endian sock_filter array -> this file.
  Captured 2026-10-23 on fev's build-host engine; 846 instructions.

Verification
  guest/debug/attach TestDefaultSeccompProgram interprets the embedded program in
  pure Go and asserts: keyctl/add_key/request_key/bpf/mount/reboot/init_module/
  kexec_load ERRNO; unshare and clone(CLONE_NEWUSER) ERRNO; read/write/openat/
  execve/clone(no new-ns flags)/brk/personality ALLOW; a foreign-arch call KILLed.

Fixed data; the compiler is beside it
  This is the fixed default program for a container with no seccomp profile of its
  own. A stopped container's own custom profile is compiled to its exact filter by
  seccompcompile.go, held equal to the engine's own
  libseccomp program decision for decision.
